## How these rules are enforced

| Layer | What it does |
|---|---|
| `lint.mjs` (PostToolUse) | Lints every file the moment it is written; findings come back to you |
| `.claude/rules/*.md` | Path-scoped detail that loads when matching files are touched |
| `gate.mjs` (Stop) | Blocks the turn from ending while typecheck fails in a unit touched this turn, committed or not |
| `node scripts/gate.mjs` | The PR gate, steps from `[gate]` in `.claude/specwright.ini`; CI runs the same command |

What no hook enforces: the load test, the leak probe, running the feature
yourself, and judgement about cost. Those live in `__DOCS_DIR__/feature-workflow.md`.

## Working agreement

- Run `node scripts/gate.mjs` before declaring work done. Do not disable any hook.
- Never add a lint-disable for a hard rule. If a rule is wrong, change the
  rule and its doc together, in the same PR, with the reason.
- When a rule conflicts with what you were about to write, the rule wins. Say
  so and propose the change rather than working around it.
